# "NOT YET" IS NOT "THERE ARE NONE".
#
# Memories are COMPUTED, by a pass that may not have run. An empty list with
# `computed: false` means nobody has looked; the screen says so, and a member
# who reads "You have no memories" instead has been told something about their
# library that the vault never established.
#
# It is the same shape as `DuplicatesData.scan_complete`, and for the same
# reason: both screens are a pass's output, both have an empty list while the
# pass is pending, and both would otherwise report the pending state as a
# finished answer. `photos-memories/computed-and-empty` is the pair that makes
# this falsifiable — one boolean apart, and only one of them may say "none".
#
# This is DATA, not a failure: the read landed, and what it returned is the
# true state of a pass that has not run. A retry does not make one run.
seat {
  availability: AVAILABILITY_READY
  durability: DURABILITY_AUTHORITATIVE
  connectivity: CONNECTIVITY_ONLINE_UNMETERED
}
data {
  computed: false
}
